  "details": "Specifically, it's turning your head up and to the side that causes this problem. It's difficult to put in words, so here is a clip demonstrating it: https://gfycat.com/ashamedbogusbufeo. In this video, any time the background moves that is unintended rotation.\nThis is a picture of the graph that it happens on:\nhttps://imgur.com/a/9dMl8X4\nAnd here is the world link:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_94a90294-ead3-4948-ab42-96297d36c7ad&instanceId=56982~private(usr_f74ae803-ad2d-4db2-9b89-367642ba7d5f)~nonce(5424bc67-262e-4737-9000-df9a1c604d63)\nThis is a problem we've had when dealing with pre-udon climbing systems, but we got around it by working with the playspace root instead of the character root. But udon does not have access to the playspace root so we would have to fall back to previous janky solutions involving multiple teleports.\nThis is the same behavior seen in this canny, but updated now that udon makes it easy to reproduce the bug: https://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/862-teleport-player-with-align-room-to-destination-false-can-rotate-the-player",
